  <h2 id="money-check">Money check before you pay</h2>

  <p>
    Our strongest suggestion: keep the total you pay for exam preparation and credential checks near a tenth of your family education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a caution that needs a clear reason. This does not apply to very cheap online learning, so look at free and low-priced practice material first.
  </p>

  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 5 lakh budget, a tenth is Rs 50,000 and a fifth is Rs 1 lakh. Keep the rest for living costs while you switch, travel, and a reserve in case the offer is delayed.
  </p>

  <p>
    General information, not financial advice; get all terms in writing and do not borrow to pay an agent. Apply on the regulator or employer website, because no agent can promise a licence, a job or a visa. Our guide on <a href="/blog/study-abroad/education-loan-for-study-abroad-india/">education loans for study abroad</a> explains why repayment that depends on a foreign job is high risk.
  </p>

